  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 836 PM MST Fri Nov 6 2026\n\nRain showers moving in tonight will increase in coverage across\nthe region, continuing into Saturday east of the Rio Grande. The\ncurrent NBM has storm total amounts around less than a quarter of\nan inch of rain for most of the area, though Hudspeth County could\nsee up to three quarters of an inch of rain through Saturday. \nRainfall rates will be light to moderate due to minimal \ninstability. Some brief mixing is possible in the Sacramento \nMountains around 9000 feet with accumulating snowfall levels \nabove 10,000 feet, and impacts will be minimal. Cloudy conditions\nand easterly winds will make high temperatures struggle to reach \n60 degrees on Saturday.\n\nQuiet weather returns on Sunday as temperatures begin their\ngradual warm up through the week. A ridge moves in from the\nPacific, advecting drier air into the region for Sunday (with the\nexception of southern Hudspeth County). A disorganized trough will\nmove through the area Tuesday night, with a spotty shower or two not\nout of the question. Expect slowly warming temperatures, back to \nnear normal (lower-70s in the lowlands), by Wednesday.",
